[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:1. A Private Conversation]
[00:00.760]Passage 1 | 文章一
[00:02.625]A private conversation | 一次私人谈话
[00:05.630]Last week, | 上周，
[00:07.545]I went to the theatre. | 我去看了戏。
[00:09.320]I had a very good seat. | 我的座位很好。
[00:11.390]The play was very interesting. | 戏演得非常精彩。
[00:14.415]I did not enjoy it. | 我却没能欣赏它。
[00:17.270]A young man and a young woman | 一个年轻人和一位年轻女子
[00:19.855]were sitting behind me. | 坐在我后面。
[00:21.535]They were talking loudly. | 他们大声地说着话。
[00:24.080]I got very angry. | 我非常生气。
[00:26.495]I could not hear the actors. | 我听不见演员的台词了。
[00:29.170]I turned round. | 我转过身来。
[00:31.290]I looked at the man and the woman angrily. | 我怒气冲冲地看了看那两个人。
[00:34.930]They did not pay any attention. | 他们却一点也不在意。
[00:38.320]In the end, I could not bear it. | 最后，我忍无可忍了。
[00:42.195]I turned round again. | 我又转过身去。
[00:44.605]I can't hear a word, | “我一个字也听不见了！”
[00:47.235]I said angrily. | 我生气地说。
[00:49.610]It's none of your business, | “这不关你的事。”
[00:52.140]the young man said rudely. | 那个年轻人粗鲁地说。
[00:54.165]This is a private conversation. | “这是私人谈话。”